0,Squamish culture - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squamish_culture,"January 10, 2026 - Squamish culture is the customs, arts, music, lifestyle, food, painting and sculpture, moral systems and social institutions of the Squamish indigenous people, located in the southwestern part of British Columbia, Canada. They refer to themselves as Sḵwx̱wú7mesh ([sqʷχʷúʔmʃ]). They are a part of the Coast Salish ...",Squamish,Salish
1,Squamish Valley Music Festival - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squamish_Valley_Music_Festival,"May 3, 2025 - The Squamish Valley Music Festival (pronounced /ˈskwɔːmɪʃ/), previously LIVE at Squamish, was an annual music festival co-produced by Vancouver-based BRANDLIVE Management and Live Nation Canada, held in Squamish, British Columbia, over the second weekend in August.",Squamish,Salish
2,Squamish language - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squamish_language,"3 weeks ago - Squamish (/ˈskwɔːmɪʃ/ SKWAW-mish; Sḵwx̱wú7mesh sníchim, sníchim meaning ""language"") is a Coast Salish language spoken by the Squamish people of the Pacific Northwest. It is spoken in southwestern British Columbia, Canada, centred on their reserve communities in Squamish, North Vancouver, ...",Squamish,Salish
3,Squamish Music & Live Arts - Facebook,https://www.facebook.com/groups/581295482349676/,"Jun 2, 2026 · A place to find all music-related gigs/events in Squamish incl. gigs, parties, festivals, open-mic’s and karaoke nights. This is also a place to post...",Squamish,Salish
4,Salish songs - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL_MQe_0PiW3_kAz8LusGDNb2tKJwx6f6P,Chief Jimmy Jimmy Welcome. Squamish Dance & Songs.,Squamish,Salish
5,Salish songs - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL_MQe_0PiW3_kAz8LusGDNb2tKJwx6f6P,"Listen to Salish songs on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more.",Squamish,Salish
6,We are Coast Salish – Tsatsu Stalqayu,http://tsatsustalqayu.ca/we-are-coast-salish/,"A traditional Salish song and dance group, the group consists of over 25 male and female members of a single family, from age 6 months to over age 50. Their variation in age and gender allows for more song, dance and stories to be shared on stage and in their presentations.",Squamish,Salish
7,Explore Coast Salish drum-making traditions - Squamish Chief,https://www.squamishchief.com/local-news/skwxxwu7mesh-nation-artist-anthony-joseph-leads-drum-making-workshop-at-capilano-university-9651245,"Oct 11, 2024 · For Joseph, he believes that drum-making has deep cultural importance in the Coast Salish community. “It’s a tradition for us. We use the drums in our longhouse,” he said. Drums can also be used for spiritual work including ceremonial singing and dancing.",Squamish,Salish
8,"Sḵwx̱wú7mesh ulh wa Lúlum - Squamish Singers, by Sḵwx̱wú7mesh ulh wa Lúlum",https://squamishsingers.bandcamp.com/album/sk-wx-wu-7mesh-ulh-wa-lu-lum-squamish-singers,"November 20, 2025 - ... The Sḵwx̱wú7meshulh wa lúlum (Squamish singers) are a group of friends and family who love to sing traditional songs of their Coast Salish ancestors, Comprised of Sḵwx̱wú7mesh úxwumixw (Squamish People) their spouses and children.",Squamish,Salish
9,Welcome Song - song and lyrics by Squamish Lil'wat Cultural Centre Ambassadors | Spotify,https://open.spotify.com/track/0CWPIPcvyf6D7UWWpWcJAW,"Salish Spirit Canoe Family · Artist · Puyallup Canoe Family · Artist · The Deer Clan Singers · Artist · Bobby Mercier · Artist · Eddie Box Sr. Artist · Lhaqtemish Canoe Family · Artist · Akwesasne Big Bear Singers · Artist · Eastern Eagle Singers · Artist · From the album · Songs from Our Nation, Vol. 3 · May 4, 2020 · © 2020 Squamish Lil'wat Cultural Centre ·",Squamish,Salish
